  "hospital_course": "Patient presented with AKI on CKD Stage 4, precipitated by self-prescribed Diclofenac. The NSAID was immediately stopped. He was managed for hyperkalaemia with IV Calcium gluconate, insulin with dextrose, and sodium bicarbonate. Fluid overload was treated with high-dose IV furosemide and fluid restriction. Ramipril was held due to AKI. Haemodialysis was discussed but declined by the patient and family. Over the course of admission, potassium levels normalized, creatinine trended down from a peak of 5.2 to 3.6 mg/dl, and urine output improved to 800ml/day. Haemoglobin remained stable.",
